# CtrlIRL-Coder pipeline template — multi-layer compositor, 1920x1080 @ 30fps
# (MPEG-TS).
#
# Layers (see a FullHD scene definition) feed the `compositor` element; this
# template has no upstream source of its own. The composited frames are
# encoded + audio-muxed to MPEG-TS and end in the same terminal sink as
# example-full.pipeline: `appsink name=appsink`, which ctrlirl-coder pulls
# (gst_app_sink_pull_sample) and sends over SRT (destination from config.toml
# [srt] uri). The appsink is also the stats surface for the adaptive bitrate
# controller (frame liveness, encoded throughput, caps framerate).
#
# This is the 30fps twin of example-layered-1080p60.pipeline: same contract
# elements, caps pinned to 1920x1080 @ 30fps. Use it with 1080p30 scenes and
# a 30fps OBS (e.g. scripts/test-obs-browser.ts); keep the 60fps twin for
# 1080p60 scenes, and example-layered.pipeline for 720p30 scenes.
#
# Contract elements:
#   compositor — multi-layer scene (layers attached via sink_%d pads)
#   appsink    — terminal sink (MANDATORY; Go pulls + sends SRT)
#   venc_kbps  — x264enc encoder (bitrate property in kbit/s)
#   mux        — mpegtsmux (browser layers attach their page audio here)

# IMPORTANT: the caps after the compositor MUST pin format + width + height +
# framerate to the scene size. The compositor (GStreamer 1.28) resolves its
# output caps from upstream video info at negotiate time; with a live appsrc
# frontend that info is not ready during preroll, so a bare `format=I420`
# (or any non-pinning caps) makes the compositor lock to its 1x1 default and
# the encoder never receives a frame. A scene larger than the pin gets squashed
# into it (a 1080p scene behind the 720p pin streams as a 1280x720 block).
# Keep width/height/framerate in sync with the scene definition.
compositor name=compositor background=black
  ! videoconvert
  ! video/x-raw,format=I420,width=1920,height=1080,framerate=30/1
  ! x264enc speed-preset=superfast tune=zerolatency bitrate=6000 key-int-max=30 name=venc_kbps
  ! h264parse config-interval=1
  ! mux.
mpegtsmux name=mux
  ! appsink name=appsink
